WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:15.272
ran upstairs to tell Molly's mom about Molly's accident.

2
00:00:16.694 --> 00:00:19.716
Mrs. O'Donnell rushed down the stairs in front of our building.

3
00:00:20.817 --> 00:00:21.818
Molly tried to get up.

4
00:00:22.919 --> 00:00:24.540
But she couldn't stand on her right foot.

5
00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:27.303
"Ow! It really hurts!"

6
00:00:27.863 --> 00:00:28.384
she cried.

7
00:00:29.624 --> 00:00:30.965
"Don't try to stand on it!"

8
00:00:31.405 --> 00:00:32.385
said Molly's mom.

9
00:00:32.405 --> 00:00:35.507
"I think we'd better take a taxi to the hospital."

10
00:00:37.848 --> 00:00:41.530
Mr. Calabria went out to the street and stopped a taxi.

11
00:00:43.570 --> 00:00:47.132
Then Molly, her mom, and Caswell got inside.

12
00:00:48.173 --> 00:00:51.174
Caswell waved to us as the taxi sped away.

13
00:00:52.715 --> 00:00:55.136
He was still licking his lime ice pop.

14
00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:02.362
Josh, Jenny, and I ran upstairs and told my mom about Molly's accident.

15
00:01:03.803 --> 00:01:05.383
A short time later, Mr.

16
00:01:05.463 --> 00:01:06.764
Chen came to our door.

17
00:01:07.884 --> 00:01:11.086
Josh and Jenny's aunt, Lydia, was with him.

18
00:01:12.406 --> 00:01:14.207
I had met Aunt Lydia before.

19
00:01:15.368 --> 00:01:16.388
She looked like Mr.

20
00:01:16.468 --> 00:01:18.089
Chen, but she was taller.

21
00:01:19.209 --> 00:01:20.650
She also laughed a lot.

22
00:01:21.850 --> 00:01:25.372
She laughed now as she leaned over to hug Josh and Jenny.

23
00:01:26.568 --> 00:01:28.889
"I want you to meet someone," she said.

24
00:01:28.909 --> 00:01:31.851
"He's waiting for you downstairs."

25
00:01:33.032 --> 00:01:34.012
She smiled at me.

26
00:01:34.032 --> 00:01:36.894
"Iggy, you can come too!"

27
00:01:38.475 --> 00:01:41.056
We went downstairs to Josh and Jenny's apartment.

28
00:01:42.297 --> 00:01:47.579
There, sitting on the kitchen table, was a cage with a brightly colored parrot!

29
00:01:47.599 --> 00:01:52.922
"This is my parrot, Tufty," Aunt Lydia said.

30
00:01:54.263 --> 00:01:55.824
She smiled at Josh and Jenny.

31
00:01:57.896 --> 00:02:00.778
"I am moving to California," she explained.

32
00:02:00.798 --> 00:02:05.460
"I can't take my Tufty with me so I'm giving him to you two."

33
00:02:06.541 --> 00:02:08.002
Jenny's eyes lit up.

34
00:02:08.022 --> 00:02:11.603
"Can we really keep Tufty, Dad?"

35
00:02:12.104 --> 00:02:12.744
she asked.

36
00:02:13.825 --> 00:02:14.885
Mr. Chen nodded.

37
00:02:14.905 --> 00:02:18.067
"Aunt Lydia says he's quiet and well-behaved."

38
00:02:19.868 --> 00:02:22.649
Bunch sniffed at the cage and wagged his tail.

39
00:02:22.669 --> 00:02:26.111
"Bunch likes Tufty!"

40
00:02:26.551 --> 00:02:27.232
said Josh.

41
00:02:28.892 --> 00:02:30.813
Aunt Lydia opened the birdcage.

42
00:02:34.656 --> 00:02:37.638
Tufty flew to Jenny and landed on her shoulder.

43
00:02:37.658 --> 00:02:40.400
"And Tufty likes me!"

44
00:02:40.940 --> 00:02:41.661
cried Jenny.

45
00:02:42.742 --> 00:02:45.464
Tufty was quiet, but he was lots of fun.

46
00:02:49.847 --> 00:02:53.609
We played with him while we waited for Molly to come home from the hospital.

47
00:02:55.290 --> 00:02:57.432
Finally we heard a car pull up.

48
00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:02.602
We ran to the window and saw a taxi.

49
00:03:03.522 --> 00:03:05.364
Molly climbed out slowly.

50
00:03:06.544 --> 00:03:08.766
She was wearing a big boot on her foot.

51
00:03:10.487 --> 00:03:13.189
Josh, Jenny, and I hurried downstairs to meet her.

52
00:03:13.209 --> 00:03:18.152
"I broke a bone in my foot," said Molly.

53
00:03:18.172 --> 00:03:22.735
"The doctor says I have to wear this walking boot until it heals."

54
00:03:22.755 --> 00:03:27.739
"If it doesn't heal, Molly will need an operation!"

55
00:03:28.259 --> 00:03:29.140
said Caswell.

56
00:03:30.248 --> 00:03:32.269
Molly nodded, looking upset.

57
00:03:32.289 --> 00:03:36.191
"The doctor would have to put screws in my foot!"

58
00:03:36.211 --> 00:03:37.911
"With Mr.

59
00:03:37.951 --> 00:03:39.512
Calabria's screwdriver?"

60
00:03:40.012 --> 00:03:41.033
asked Caswell.

61
00:03:42.213 --> 00:03:43.474
Molly rolled her eyes.

62
00:03:43.494 --> 00:03:47.296
"No, Caswell," she said.

63
00:03:47.316 --> 00:03:50.317
"The doctor isn't going to use Mr.

64
00:03:50.357 --> 00:03:51.998
Calabria's screwdriver."

65
00:03:52.758 --> 00:03:53.698
Molly frowned.

66
00:03:53.718 --> 00:03:56.980
"I don't want an operation!"

67
00:03:58.572 --> 00:04:00.293
We told Molly about Tufty.

68
00:04:02.113 --> 00:04:04.554
Then we all went upstairs to Molly's apartment.

69
00:04:06.014 --> 00:04:10.475
Molly walked very slowly, taking one step at a time.

70
00:04:14.816 --> 00:04:15.277
what Dr.

71
00:04:15.317 --> 00:04:17.257
Chang said, Molly," said Mrs.

72
00:04:17.337 --> 00:04:20.598
O'Donnell. "You have to take care of your foot.

73
00:04:21.678 --> 00:04:25.299
And if you keep your spirits up, that will help your foot to heal quickly.

74
00:04:25.839 --> 00:04:27.580
Then you won't need an operation."

75
00:04:28.864 --> 00:04:31.466
"What does 'keeping your spirits up' mean?"

76
00:04:31.966 --> 00:04:32.606
asked Jenny.

77
00:04:32.626 --> 00:04:37.909
"It means staying happy and cheerful," said Molly's mom.

78
00:04:37.929 --> 00:04:43.432
"It's hard to be cheerful with this walking boot on," Molly complained.

79
00:04:43.452 --> 00:04:46.774
"It makes my leg hot and itchy."

80
00:04:47.894 --> 00:04:49.996
She leaned over and scratched her leg.

81
00:04:50.016 --> 00:04:56.539
"Iggy, think of something to help Molly stay cheerful," said Caswell.

82
00:04:56.559 --> 00:04:59.097
"Yeah!" said Josh.

83
00:04:59.117 --> 00:05:01.718
"You have to invent something for her."

84
00:05:01.738 --> 00:05:05.621
"Something wonderful," added Jenny.

85
00:05:05.641 --> 00:05:09.724
"And different," said Molly.

86
00:05:10.905 --> 00:05:12.466
Everyone was looking at me.

87
00:05:12.486 --> 00:05:15.728
"Oh boy," I thought.

88
00:05:16.929 --> 00:05:20.231
My friends really believed in me and my powers of invention.

89
00:05:21.332 --> 00:05:24.054
Now I had to think of something to help Molly!
